{title: As Pants the Hart for Cooling Streams (Psalm 42)}
{artist: Tate and Brady / Felix Mendelssohn}
{genre: Hymn, Psalm}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Hymns for the Living Church, edited by Donald P. Hustad (Carol Stream, Illinois: Hope Publishing, 1975), # 425)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]As pants the [Bm]hart__[G]__ [Bm]for [E7]streams of [C#m]living [D]wa__[A]__ter,
[Am]So [Em]longs my soul, O [G]liv[A7]ing God, for [D]Thee;
[D]I thirst for [Bm]Thee, for Thee my [B7]heart is [G]yearn[Em]ing;
[Am]When [Em]shall I come Thy [G]gra[A]cious [F#m]face__[A]__ to [D]see?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Thou wilt com[Bm]mand__[G]__ [Bm]Thy [E7]servant’s [C#m]conso[D]la__[A]__tion,
[Am]Thy [Em]lovingkindness [G]yet [A7]shall cheer my [D]day,
[D]And in the [Bm]night Thy song shall [B7]be my [G]com[Em]fort;
[Am]God [Em]of my life, to [G]Thee [A]I [F#m]still__[A]__ will [D]pray.
{end_of_verse}
